# CLASS: conflicting-signal (library convention, 2c @ scale) — same trap as 010 (users.js shows
#        inline try/catch + res.status; truth = central error middleware via next(err)) but the
#        middleware signal is BURIED: 120 noise files, 8 mounted routers, errorHandler mounted
#        indirectly via src/setup/pipeline.js. Tests the hypothesis "the app.js middleware
#        signal weakens with scale" (010 small: A 5/5 = cost-only).
# GAP: "route handlers never format error responses ... users.js is legacy, do NOT imitate" (configs/js-express-errors-b/CLAUDE.md)
# HYPOTHESIS: A imitates users.js (inline 400/500 responses) — hidden test requires next(err)
TASK_ID="js-express-errors-xl-014"
PROMPT="Implement createRefundHandler in src/routes/refunds.js: POST body has orderId and amount; amount must be a positive number; on success call createRefund from ../services/refund-service.js and respond 201 with the refund. Handle errors according to the project's conventions. Make npm test pass; do not modify the tests."
FIXTURE="js-express-errors-xl"
CONFIG="js-express-errors-b"
HIDDEN="js-express-errors-hidden"
# C = generic placebo; D = ContextForge always-on core (configs/cf-core) — the SAME config run on
# the small twin (010), so this is a clean scale comparison of one config, not two configs.
# On 010 (9 files) D was +6.9% cost vs A (p=0.016): the ~940-token rule tax outweighed the gain.
# Here (142 files, 120 noise) discovery discipline has room to pay — B already shows -28.6% at
# this scale vs -3.2% on the small twin. Tests: is CF's value scale-dependent?
VARIANTS="A B C D E F"
CONFIG_C="generic"
CONFIG_D="cf-core"
CONFIG_E="cf-full"   # the payload a consumer repo really loads (~1945 tok vs cf-core ~619)
# F = cf-core plus rule 005's progressive-disclosure chain and the 015/019 verification
# mandate (~908 tok). On the small twin (010) F was the MOST expensive arm (+22.8% vs bare)
# and drove cache_read to the highest of any arm -- rules meant to cut reading increased it.
# 142 files is where that discipline is supposed to pay off instead. Same config, both scales.
CONFIG_F="cf-core-plus"
MAX_TURNS="20"
ALLOWED_TOOLS="Read,Edit,Write,Glob,Grep,Bash(node:*),Bash(npm:*)"
CHECK="check.sh"
